---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';

const h2 = 'mt-12 text-2xl font-bold tracking-[-0.01em] text-charcoal first:mt-0';
const p = 'mt-4 text-[17px] leading-[1.7] text-gray-muted';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — TBM"
  description="How TBM Ventures LLC collects, uses, and protects information."
>
  <Section id="privacy" padding="pt-section-mobile pb-section-mobile md:pt-section md:pb-section">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-text">
      <h1 class="text-[36px] font-bold leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-charcoal md:text-[40px]">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-muted">
        Effective August 14, 2026. TBM Ventures LLC ("TBM," "we," "us").
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Overview</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        This policy covers two things: how we handle information from visitors to this
        website, and how we handle information that passes through the screening systems we
        build and run for client law firms. If you're a prospective client firm, this is what
        to expect. If you're someone who submitted a screening form on a campaign we run for
        one of our client firms, the "Information from client campaigns" section below applies
        to you.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Information this website collects</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        This site does not use cookies, analytics, or tracking scripts, and it does not run
        any advertising pixels. We don't collect anything automatically when you browse it.
      </p>
      <p class={p}>
        If you click "Book a Strategy Call," you're taken to Cal.com, a third-party scheduling
        tool, to pick a time and provide your name, email, and whatever you choose to share
        about your firm. That's governed by Cal.com's own privacy policy, not this one. If you
        email us directly, we keep that correspondence to respond to you and, if you become a
        client, to service the engagement.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Information from client campaigns</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        When we run a case-category campaign for a client law firm, the screening forms we
        build collect information relevant to that firm's intake: case category, jurisdiction,
        filing history, contact details, and language preference. That information is
        collected on behalf of, and for the benefit of, the retaining firm — it is routed to
        their calendar and their intake process. We do not sell it, and we do not share it with
        any other firm. It is used only to operate the screening and nurture system described
        on this site for the firm that collected it.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>How we use information</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        To respond to inquiries, to deliver the services a client firm has contracted for, to
        route qualified consultations to the correct calendar, and to keep the compliance and
        billing records the engagement requires.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Sharing</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        We do not sell personal information. We share it only with the service providers
        necessary to run the system — ad platforms, scheduling and messaging tools (email,
        SMS, WhatsApp) — each governed by their own privacy terms, and, for campaign leads,
        with the client firm that the campaign was run for.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Your rights</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        To access, correct, or request deletion of information we hold about you, email
        <a href="mailto:ben@thebenmount.com" class="border-b border-blue/30 text-blue">
          ben@thebenmount.com
        </a>. If you submitted a form on a client firm's campaign, we can route that request to
        the firm as well, since they hold the underlying case relationship.
        {'{{TODO: add state-specific disclosures (e.g. CCPA) once client geography is known}}'}
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        If this policy changes, we'll update the effective date above. Material changes will
        be reflected here before they take effect.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Contact</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Questions about this policy: <a
          href="mailto:ben@thebenmount.com"
          class="border-b border-blue/30 text-blue">ben@thebenmount.com</a
        >. This policy is governed by the laws of {'{{TODO: governing state}}'}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>
